{"task_id": "Mbpp/18", "solution": "def remove_dirty_chars(source_string: str, chars_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes characters from source_string that are present in chars_to_remove.\n\n    Args:\n        source_string: The original string from which characters will be removed.\n        chars_to_remove: A string containing characters to be excluded.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new string with specified characters removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine if character is present in chars_to_remove efficiently using a set.\n    chars_to_remove_set = set(chars_to_remove)\n\n    result_chars = []\n    # Iterate through each character of the source string.\n    for char in source_string:\n        # If the character is NOT present in the set of characters to be removed, append it.\n        if char not in chars_to_remove_set:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n\n    # Return a new string composed of the filtered characters.\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
