{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "def index_minimum(tuple_list: list[tuple]) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value in a list of tuples.\n    If multiple tuples share the minimum second value, the first one encountered is chosen.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return None\n\n    min_second_value = float('inf')\n    result_first_value = None\n\n    for current_tuple in tuple_list:\n        # Assuming each tuple has at least two elements and the second element is comparable\n        first_val = current_tuple[0]\n        second_val = current_tuple[1]\n\n        if second_val < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = second_val\n            result_first_value = first_val\n            \n    return result_first_value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the digits of a number follow an 'abab...' undulating pattern.\n    Requires at least three digits and the first two digits must be different.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_number = str(number)\n\n    if len(s_number) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    if s_number[0] == s_number[1]:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(2, len(s_number)):\n        if s_number[i] != s_number[i - 2]:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
