{"task_id": "Mbpp/95", "solution": "def Find_Min_Length(input_list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the smallest list in a list of lists.\n    Assumes valid input as per the design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    for inner_list in input_list_of_lists:\n        min_length = min(min_length, len(inner_list))\n    return int(min_length)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "import math\n\ndef divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of divisors for a given positive integer n.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of n\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            # i is a divisor\n            count += 1\n            # If i*i != n, then n/i is another distinct divisor\n            if i * i != n:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
