{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "def reverse_vowels(input_string: str) -> str:\n    # Helper function to check if a character is a vowel (case-insensitive, 'y' is not a vowel).\n    _VOWELS = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    def _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        return char.lower() in _VOWELS\n\n    char_list = list(input_string)\n    vowel_indices = []\n    vowels_found = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(char_list):\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n            vowels_found.append(char)\n\n    # Reverse the list of found vowels\n    vowels_found.reverse()\n\n    # Place the reversed vowels back into their original vowel positions\n    for i, vowel_index in enumerate(vowel_indices):\n        char_list[vowel_index] = vowels_found[i]\n\n    return \"\".join(char_list)"}
