{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(elements: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(elements)  # Create a mutable copy of the input list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in arr[0...curr_size-1]\n        max_idx = arr.index(max(arr[:curr_size]))\n\n        # Move the maximum element to the beginning\n        # (if it's not already there)\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # First, flip the sub-array from 0 to max_idx\n            arr[:max_idx + 1] = arr[:max_idx + 1][::-1]\n\n            # Second, flip the sub-array from 0 to curr_size-1\n            arr[:curr_size] = arr[:curr_size][::-1]\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/140", "solution": "def extract_singly(list_of_tuples: list[tuple]) -> set[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flattens a list of tuples into a set of unique numbers.\n    It iterates through each tuple and adds its elements to a set to ensure uniqueness.\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_numbers = set()\n    for tpl in list_of_tuples:\n        for num in tpl:\n            unique_numbers.add(num)\n    return unique_numbers"}
