{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\ndef sum_range_list(numbers: List[Union[int, float]], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified 0-based inclusive range.\n    Raises ValueError for invalid index inputs based on design constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    # Validate indices against the list's bounds.\n    if not (0 <= start_index < n and 0 <= end_index < n):\n        raise ValueError(\"Indices must be within the list's bounds.\")\n\n    # Validate that the start index is not greater than the end index.\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        raise ValueError(\"Start index cannot be greater than end index.\")\n\n    current_sum = 0\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        current_sum += numbers[i]\n\n    return current_sum"}
