{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(sorted_array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given element is a majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], arr_len: int, x: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the index of the first occurrence of x in arr using binary search.\n        Returns -1 if x is not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        low = 0\n        high = arr_len - 1\n        result = -1\n\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > x\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def _find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], arr_len: int, x: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the index of the last occurrence of x in arr using binary search.\n        Returns -1 if x is not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        low = 0\n        high = arr_len - 1\n        result = -1\n\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > x\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(sorted_array, n, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(sorted_array, n, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
