{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than a given number. Handles negative inputs by returning 0.\"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Calculate the integer square root (floor(sqrt(number)))\n    root = math.isqrt(number)\n    \n    # The next perfect square will be the square of (root + 1)\n    # This covers cases where 'number' itself is a perfect square or not.\n    next_root = root + 1\n    return next_root * next_root"}
