{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "def and_tuples(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise bitwise AND operation on two input tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first input tuple of integers.\n        tuple2: The second input tuple of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the results of the element-wise bitwise AND operations.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input tuples do not have the same number of elements.\n        TypeError: If any element in the input tuples is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        element1 = tuple1[i]\n        element2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(element1, int) or not isinstance(element2, int):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Elements at index {i} must be integers. Got {type(element1).__name__} and {type(element2).__name__}.\")\n\n        result.append(element1 & element2)\n\n    return tuple(result)"}
