{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "class Trapezium:\n    \"\"\"Represents a trapezium with two parallel bases.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, base1: float, base2: float):\n        \"\"\"Initializes a Trapezium object and validates base lengths.\"\"\"\n        if base1 <= 0 or base2 <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Bases must be positive numbers.\")\n        self._base1 = base1\n        self._base2 = base2\n\n    def get_median_length(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the median length of the trapezium.\"\"\"\n        return (self._base1 + self._base2) / 2\n\ndef median_trapezium(base1: float, base2: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium.\n    This function internally uses a Trapezium class to encapsulate the logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    trapezium_obj = Trapezium(base1, base2)\n    return trapezium_obj.get_median_length()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/437", "solution": "def remove_odd(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes characters at odd 1-based positions from the input string.\n    This means characters at 0-based indices 0, 2, 4, etc., are removed, and characters at 0-based indices 1, 3, 5, etc., are kept.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_string)):\n        if (i + 1) % 2 == 0:  # Check if 1-based position (i+1) is even\n            result.append(input_string[i])\n    return \"\".join(result)"}
