{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def _validate_n(n: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates if n is a positive natural number.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive natural number.\")\n\ndef _calculate_sum_n(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the first n natural numbers (BR2).\"\"\"\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2\n\ndef _calculate_sum_cubes_n(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first n natural numbers (BR3).\"\"\"\n    sum_n = _calculate_sum_n(n)\n    return sum_n * sum_n\n\ndef difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first n natural numbers (FR1, BR4).\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_n(n)\n\n    sum_n = _calculate_sum_n(n)\n    sum_cubes_n = _calculate_sum_cubes_n(n)\n\n    return sum_cubes_n - sum_n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(numbers: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs in a list of integers whose XOR value is odd.\n    An XOR value is odd if and only if one integer is odd and the other is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(list_length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, list_length):\n            num1 = numbers[i]\n            num2 = numbers[j]\n\n            # Check if one number is odd and the other is even\n            if (num1 % 2) != (num2 % 2):\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
