{"task_id": "Mbpp/562", "solution": "class LengthCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the core logic for finding the maximum length among sublists.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_max_length(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the length of the longest sublist in a given list of lists.\n        Returns 0 if the input list_of_lists is empty or contains no sublists.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not list_of_lists:\n            return 0\n\n        max_length = 0\n        for sublist in list_of_lists:\n            current_length = len(sublist)\n            if current_length > max_length:\n                max_length = current_length\n        return max_length\n\ndef Find_Max_Length(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public API function to find the length of the longest sublist.\n    This function delegates the core logic to the LengthCalculator.\n    \"\"\"\n    return LengthCalculator.find_max_length(list_of_lists)"}
