{"task_id": "Mbpp/588", "solution": "def big_diff(numbers: list) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the largest and smallest numerical values in a list.\n    Handles empty lists and non-numerical values by raising exceptions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"List must contain only numerical values (int or float).\")\n\n    largest_value = max(numbers)\n    smallest_value = min(numbers)\n    return largest_value - smallest_value"}
