{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "def toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles bits of the number except the first (MSB) and the last (LSB) bit.\n    For numbers 0 or 1, there are no middle bits, so the number is returned unchanged.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return number\n\n    # Determine the position of the Most Significant Bit (MSB).\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Determine the position of the Least Significant Bit (LSB).\n    lsb_pos = (number & -number).bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Calculate the range of bits to toggle: from (LSB_pos + 1) to (MSB_pos - 1).\n    start_toggle_pos = lsb_pos + 1\n    end_toggle_pos = msb_pos - 1\n\n    middle_mask = 0\n    if start_toggle_pos <= end_toggle_pos:\n        # Create a mask with 1s for the middle bits, then shift to the correct position.\n        length = end_toggle_pos - start_toggle_pos + 1\n        middle_mask = ((1 << length) - 1) << start_toggle_pos\n\n    # Toggle the middle bits using a bitwise XOR operation.\n    return number ^ middle_mask"}
