{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions.\n\n    Handles empty lists and calculates effective rotation positions using modulo.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    effective_positions = positions % list_length\n\n    # If effective_positions is 0, no rotation is needed\n    if effective_positions == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    # Split the list into two parts\n    split_point = list_length - effective_positions\n    \n    tail = input_list[split_point:]\n    head = input_list[:split_point]\n\n    return tail + head"}
