{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "def check_expression(expression_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given expression string has balanced delimiters.\n\n    Returns True if the expression is balanced, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    opening_brackets = \"({[\"\n    closing_brackets = \")}]\"\n    bracket_map = {\")\": \"(\", \"]\": \"[\", \"}\": \"{\"}\n\n    stack = []\n\n    for char in expression_string:\n        if char in opening_brackets:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in closing_brackets:\n            if not stack or stack[-1] != bracket_map[char]:\n                return False\n            stack.pop()\n\n    return not stack"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/778", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\n\ndef pack_consecutive_duplicates(input_list: List[Any]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Packs consecutive duplicates of list elements into sublists.\n    Returns a new list of sublists, where each sublist contains consecutive identical elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    output_list: List[List[Any]] = []\n    current_sublist: List[Any] = [input_list[0]]\n\n    for item in input_list[1:]:\n        if item == current_sublist[-1]:\n            current_sublist.append(item)\n        else:\n            output_list.append(current_sublist)\n            current_sublist = [item]\n\n    output_list.append(current_sublist)  # Append the last sublist\n    return output_list\n```"}
