{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is strictly smaller than its\n    corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        return False\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if not (tuple2[i] < tuple1[i]):\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "solution": "import math\n\ndef _is_perfect_square(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a positive integer is a perfect square.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return False\n    if n == 0:\n        return True\n\n    sqrt_n = int(math.isqrt(n))\n    return sqrt_n * sqrt_n == n\n\ndef count_divisors(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the count of positive divisors for a number is even.\"\"\"\n    return not _is_perfect_square(number)"}
